<title>BRAZIL: Bovespa sees 84.9 mln real outflows so far in June.</title>
<headline>Bovespa sees 84.9 mln real outflows so far in June.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange (Bovespa) said it has registered net foreign capital outflows of 84.9 million reais in the first 10 days of June.</p>
<p>Foreign buys totaled 1.648 billion reais, while foreign sales amounted to 1.733 billion reais in the period, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>In May, the bolsa posted net foreign inflows of 259.3 million reais.</p>
<p>So far this year, net foreign investment in the bolsa totalled 1.341 billion reais, it said.</p>
<p>((-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413)</p>
